REJECTED — DO NOT APPLY.

I drafted this patch, tested it, and it is wrong. Kept as the record of a
refuted hypothesis, because the refutation is the useful part.

THE HYPOTHESIS
  warn_unpromoted_write_scope() excludes `return_artifact` from its
  check (`extra = [p for p in paths if p and p != ret]`). Promotion of
  other write_scope paths runs through commit_worker_residue(), which
  enumerates residue with:
      git status --porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all
  and no --ignored, so it cannot see a gitignored file. I inferred that a
  gitignored `return_artifact` would therefore also be dropped silently,
  unguarded, and that the exemption was an oversight.

WHY IT IS WRONG
  Two measurements killed it.

  1. The exemption is not reachable as a defect, because the NORMAL
     artifact path is already gitignored for every board task:
       $ git check-ignore -v departments/shared/outbox/TASK-...-response.md
       .gitignore:26:departments/*/outbox/*.md  departments/shared/outbox/...
       $ git ls-files 'departments/*/outbox/*' | wc -l
       0
     Applied to a copy, this patch fired on all four fixtures including
     the clean positive control. It is not a guard, it is a constant.

  2. The artifact never goes through git at all. bin/board-supervisor.sh
     promotes it with publish_prepared_worktree_outputs() (line 2177) — a
     direct file bridge — and passes both output paths as exclude_paths to
     commit_worker_residue() and integrate_worktree_commits()
     (lines ~2145-2165):
         exclude_paths=(
             authority["expected_result_path"],
             authority["expected_outbox_path"],
         )
     So the artifact's ignore status is irrelevant by construction. The
     exemption in warn_unpromoted_write_scope is CORRECT BY DESIGN: the one
     path git cannot carry is precisely the one the bridge carries instead.

STANDING CONCLUSION
  No change to bin/send-task.sh is warranted. The guard is right as written.
  tools/wsguard/verify.sh C5 now asserts this exemption rather than treating
  it as a gap, and C6 pins the supervisor exclusion that justifies it.

